00:04:19,090 --> 00:04:25,090
The inside story of the painting that seduced the world.

2
00:08:38,181 --> 00:08:44,181
The Lost Leonardo is a documentary, history film directed by Andreas Koefoed.

3
00:12:57,272 --> 00:13:03,272
London, England, 2008.

4
00:17:16,363 --> 00:17:22,363
Some of the most distinguished experts on the work of Italian artist Leonardo da Vinci (1452-1519) gather at the National Gallery to examine a
painting known as Salvator Mundi; an event that turns out to be the first act of one of the most fascinating stories in the history of art.

5
00:21:35,454 --> 00:21:41,454
Self - Writer and Journalist, played by Georgina Adam.

6
00:25:54,545 --> 00:26:00,545
Self - Art Dealer, played by Warren Adelson.

7
00:30:13,636 --> 00:30:19,636
Self - Banker, played by Evan Beard.

8
00:34:32,727 --> 00:34:38,727
Self - Freeport Owner and Businessman, played by Yves Bouvier.

9
00:38:51,818 --> 00:38:57,818
Self - Writer, played by Alexandra Bregman.

10
00:43:10,909 --> 00:43:16,909
Self - Editor, played by Alison Cole.

11
00:47:29,999 --> 00:47:35,999
The Lost Leonardo is an internationally co-produced documentary
film directed by Andreas Koefoed, released in 2021.

12
00:51:49,090 --> 00:51:55,090
It follows the discovery and successive sales of the painting the Salvator Mundi, allegedly a work by
Leonardo da Vinci, an artist for whom there are only a few attributed works in existence.

13
00:56:08,181 --> 00:56:14,181
The film chronicles the dramatic increases in the painting's value from its original purchase in 2005 for $1,175
to its auction in 2017 for $450 million, when it became the most expensive artwork ever sold.

14
01:00:27,272 --> 01:00:33,272
The use of high-end artwork for hiding wealth, as well as the conflicts created by
large commissions and other economic incentives, are explored in the film.

15
01:04:46,363 --> 01:04:52,363
It includes interviews with leading art experts and art critics on issues
regarding the provenance and authenticity of the work.

16
01:09:05,454 --> 01:09:11,454
Production was announced in late 2019 following the success of Ben Lewis's book The
Last Leonardo: The Secret Lives of the World’s Most Expensive Painting.

17
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
The film had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on June 13, 2021, and was released in the United States on
August 13, 2021, by Sony Pictures Classics and in the United Kingdom on September 10, 2021, by Dogwoof.

18
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
The film was widely praised by critics for its content, pacing
and the portrayal of the subject as a thriller.

19
01:22:02,727 --> 01:22:08,727
A French-made film on the topic called The Saviour for
Sale was also released at the same time.

20
01:26:21,818 --> 01:26:27,818
In October 2022, StudioCanal announced a plan to develop the film into a
limited series with The Picture Company and Entertainment360.

21
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
The film explores themes of painting, leonardo da vinci,
based on true story, art, art auction.
